# text
seg-9b505908a6e2 = Kshana <b>drives no radio hardware and transmits nothing</b>. It includes a software GNSS receiver for recorded and generated IQ, and can write synthetic baseband IQ files, but it is <b>not RF signal-generator hardware</b> and <b>not a hardware or certified GNSS receiver</b>. It is a study and trade-off instrument: it simulates what jamming, spoofing and signal loss do to a navigation and timing solution, and tells you which of its answers are validated. <b>Not a flight product.</b>
